BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Living with Music: Black Authors on the Music That Shapes Their Wr
 iting\, with Authors Morgan Campbell and I. Augustus Durham
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T203000
UID:bm-5591520260625@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/Living_wi
 th_Music.jpg?cb=1780412021
DESCRIPTION:Come celebrate Black Music Month (June) at A Different Booklis
 t! We'll be presenting a conversation between local authors Morgan Campbel
 l (MY FIGHTING FAMILY) and I. Augustus Durham (STAY BLACK AND DIE). They w
 ill be discussing how Black music and artists like Oscar Peterson\, Marvin
  Gaye\, Kendrick Lamar\, and many others\, shape their writing. Who influe
 nces your writing and your creative work? Free admission. All are welcome!
LOCATION:779 Bathurst St.
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
